o Correctional Facility for  smoking pot this is insane but the ACLU  has done a very good job of perpetuating  this myth you have to work really hard  to get into prison I mean really hard  it's a Lifetime Achievement Award for  persistence in criminal offending and to  end up in federal prison you have to be  a serious drug trafficker uh less than  1% of all federal drug prisoners are  there for possession and virtually all  of those possession cases have been pled  down from trafficking I take my cue from  the people in the communities that live  with open-air drug markets and what they  to the police is we want the dealers off  the streets I don't know how the police  are supposed to respond to that but if  you if you don't live in that situation  you don't know what it's like because  drug dealing is has always an implicit  threat of violence even if they're not  using guns at that moment their  territory is implicitly being controlled  by violence and people don't want it  federal sentencing reform to be honest  I'm willing to talk about tweaking the  mandatory minimum sentences because  they're all arbitrary it's not as if  there is some Platonic ideal for what a  cocaine sentence should be so if it's if  it's 20 years mandatory now for a  massive quantity that was if it had been  15 to begin with nobody would be  complaining about moving it from 20 to  15 so I'm not going to get too hot under  the collar about maybe revisiting some  of the federal penalties what I think is  more dangerous is the ideology that  underlies our current reform efforts  which is that the disproportionate  representation of blacks is in prison is  due to racism and not to criminal  offending and what we should be talking  about is how to get more black boys  fathers so they don't end up in federal  prison in the first place so I think I  think Matthew said that's thank you so  much I appreciate it  okay
 

